NAME
    man - show a manual page

SYNOPSIS
    man [name]

DESCRIPTION
    Shows the manual page for a command, a shell built-in or a library:
    the plain-text file /MAN/NAME, the name upper-cased (the pages are
    installed in upper case, so man cat reads /MAN/CAT). The page goes
    through the --More-- pager (see pager): after 23 lines a key, read
    without echo: space or any other key = the next page, Enter = one
    more line, q or Q (or Ctrl-D) = quit.

    With no name man lists the pages in /MAN, six to a row, in lower
    case. An unknown name prints "no manual entry for NAME". man is
    /BIN/MAN.

EXAMPLES
    man             the list of pages
    man dir         the page for dir
    man man         this page
    man regex       the regex dialect of grep, sed and awk
    man mon         the ROM monitor

NOTES
    On the instruction-level emulator a lower-case q is read as end of
    input, which quits as well.
    Changed from the P8X version: /MAN instead of /man with the name
    upper-cased, the pager (the P8X streamed the page whole), and the
    list when no name is given.
    Ported from P8X os/commands/man.c 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
